## 13. SEO, Accessibility and Performance

### SEO

Implement:
- Unique titles and descriptions.
- Canonical URLs.
- XML sitemap.
- Robots configuration.
- Open Graph metadata.
- Appropriate structured data for books, products, articles, and authors where supported by the relevant schema.
- Clean URLs.
- Descriptive image alternatives.
- Internal links between related books and articles.
- Correct handling of missing and redirected routes.

Do not add fabricated reviews, ratings, availability, or structured-data claims.

### Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA where feasible.

Include:
- Semantic HTML.
- Keyboard access.
- Visible focus states.
- Accessible form labels.
- Sufficient color contrast.
- Screen-reader-friendly validation and status messages.
- Alternative text for meaningful images.
- Responsive text sizing.
- Reduced-motion support.
- Accessible Devanagari reading layouts.

### Performance

Implement:
- Responsive images.
- Appropriate image formats.
- Lazy loading below the fold.
- Font optimization.
- Caching where appropriate.
- Efficient queries.
- Server-side pagination for larger catalogues.
- Minimal unnecessary client-side JavaScript.
- Appropriate loading and error states.

Measure performance on real mobile-sized viewports and representative low-bandwidth conditions.

